THE MIT LICENCE ABOVE COVERS THIS PROJECT'S SOURCE CODE AND ITS OWN ARTWORK.

  * the Lua under `ui/`, plus `questmarks-ui.lua`, `model.lua`, `notes.lua` and
    `resnames.lua`;
  * everything under `tools/`;
  * the project's own documentation;
  * and the artwork this project made for itself: `assets/papyrus.png` and the
    two page sheets derived from it, and `assets/book_closed.png` and
    `assets/book_open.png`, which are a commission drawn for this addon and in
    which no third party holds rights.

ONE SET OF FILES IS NOT UNDER IT.

    assets/category/*.png     17 region badges
    assets/category/SOURCES.json
    tools/category-sources/icons/manifest.json

Those badges are derived from BG Wiki's own category images and BG Wiki content
is CC BY-NC-SA 3.0. They are therefore offered under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, and so is
any further derivative of them. The two records beside them name, per file,
where each came from.

  Source:   https://www.bg-wiki.com
  Licence:  CC BY-NC-SA 3.0  --  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/

Because those files are NON-COMMERCIAL, questmarks-ui AS A WHOLE cannot be sold
or bundled into anything monetised, including an ad-supported distribution. The
MIT grant above still says what it says about the code; it cannot make the
badges commercial.

A limit worth stating here as well as in NOTICE: most of the wiki's category
images are SQUARE ENIX promotional or in-game artwork uploaded to the wiki, and
SQUARE ENIX's copyright in that artwork is a separate question from BG Wiki's
CC licence over its pages. A fan wiki cannot license someone else's artwork to
you.

NOTICE is the authoritative, field-by-field account of where each piece came
from, and it carries the attribution CC BY asks for. questmarks' own NOTICE
covers the quest and mission data this addon reads off your disk and applies
unchanged here.
